    "body": "`zero_wrapper_for_fp_tensor_constructor` unconditionally casts every floating-point result to `target_fp_dtype` (e.g. bfloat16), even when the caller passed an explicit `dtype=torch.float`. This silently corrupts RoPE `inv_freq` in transformers models under ZeRO-3: the `torch.arange(..., dtype=torch.float)` inside rotary embedding init is computed in bfloat16, producing angle errors of ~118 rad at position 65536.\n\n**Fix:** skip the cast when the caller passed a non-None `dtype` kwarg. The same guard is added to `get_new_tensor_fn_for_dtype` for consistency.\n\n**Testing:** added `tests/unit/runtime/zero/test_zero_init_preserve_dtype.py` covering explicit float32/float64, no-dtype, `dtype=None`, integer dtypes, and multiple creation functions (`empty`, `zeros`, `ones`, `randn`).\n\nFixes #8948",
    "changed_files": 2,
